</gif></picture><run
><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>3.  If you later edit anything in the Financial Coding 1 information, you must update the the Financial Coding 2 documents that are affected.  These are not updated automatically!!  As an example, if you change a G/L code from "computer" to "IT Desktop Computer" you will need to edit the Financial Coding 2 document under capital that will be affected by the change.  It will hold the "computer" G/L until it is changed and if  someone tries to use "computer" as their G/L it will generate an error message telling them that it cannot find the entry in the index (or something to that effect!).</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>Financial Coding 2</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>The Financial Coding 2 documents are necessary for the proper functioning of the "</run><run
><font style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Generate Financial Code</run><run
><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>" button on the Order form.  The order of determination for financial coding is </run><run
><font style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Category-&gt;Funding Source-&gt;GL Account &amp; Program Activity &amp; Project Number</run><run
><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>To create Financial Coding 2 documents, click on "Financial Coding 2" in the Admin section of the database, then click on "New Type" on the Action Bar.  All information MUST be filled.  The </run><run
><font style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Special Project Account</run><run
><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/> toggles the Program Activity &amp; GL Account switch.  For non-SPA accounts, the PA appears before the GL in the generated financial code.  For SPA accounts, the GL appears before the PA.  The </run><run
><font style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>GST Exempt</run><run
><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/> field determines whether or not to add GST to an order.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>The GL Account, Program Activity, and Internal Order/Project # fields get their values from </run><run
><font style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Financial Coding 1</run><run
><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>. Thus, before creating Financial Coding 2 documents, ensure that the GL account, Program Activity and Internal Order/Project # fields are as complete as possible.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<pardef id='3' leftmargin='1.1417in' rightmargin='73%' firstlineleftmargin='0.8118in'/>
<par def='3'><run><font style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>N.B.  It is important that only one document be created for each combination of Category and Funding Source, and that all GL/PA/IO for these combinations appear here.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
